module std_method_body.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: `hash` is a std method declared `extern "nova"` -- no body
// in std's text -- and the shell novac links against does not carry it, so
// there is nothing to call and nothing to make the call from. The subset says
// this by name instead of emitting C that cannot link. Since 2026-10-02 (task 4
// of 274) a std method WITH a handed body is made by novac (pos_2,
// `to_ascii_lower`, this fixture's carrier until that day), so the seeded cause
// moved to a method that has none.
//
// The local below is the CASCADE probe, and it is the point of this fixture:
// until 2026-08-20 the gate "was anything refused?" asked the file's whole
// diagnostic count, so a refusal HERE made `@type_bind` skip its `@scope.bind`
// in `main`, and `n` came back as a second, false diagnostic -- "unknown name"
// about a name that is bound one line above.
// NOVAC_EXPECT carries no `hash` for str
fn h(s str) -> u64 => s.hash()

fn main() {
    ro n = 1
    println(n)
}
